  <!-- ============ SECTION 21 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s21"><span class="num">21</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="three-col">
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Gesamtkostenverfahren</div><div class="glossary-def">Total cost method — organising GuV expenses by their nature (materials, personnel, depreciation).</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Umsatzkostenverfahren</div><div class="glossary-def">Cost of sales method — organising GuV expenses by their function (production, selling, administration).</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Bestandsveränderungen</div><div class="glossary-def">Changes in finished/unfinished goods inventory, an adjusting item specific to the Gesamtkostenverfahren.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Rohergebnis</div><div class="glossary-def">Gross result — a combined figure small/medium corporations may present under §276's relief.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Außerordentlich</div><div class="glossary-def">"Extraordinary" — a GuV category abolished by BilMoG 2009, now replaced by Anhang disclosure for unusually significant items.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Umsatzerlöse</div><div class="glossary-def">Revenue — amounts from sales, rentals, or leasing typical of the enterprise's ordinary business activities.</div></div>
